    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d262-a1">

                <pb facs="0317" n="1051" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg1051"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in No. 407.]</seg></opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Neill to Señor
                            Larrabrue.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Lima</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1892-07-27"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">July 27,
                    1892</hi>.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Minister</hi>: I would respectfully call the
                    attention of your excellency to the various notes from this legation as to the
                    character of the claim known as the Hydro-graphic Commission of the Amazon.</p>
                <p>I would earnestly request your excellency to have this claim again presented
                    before the honorable Congress of Peru during the present session for its early
                    consideration.</p>
                <p>I express the hope that some action will soon be taken to facilitate the early
                    and final settlement of this long-pending claim of citizens of the United States
                    upon the Government of Peru.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Richard R. Neill.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
